uped.sort(key=lambda e: e['last_trial'])\n    memory = []\n    signatures = []\n    for e in deduped:\n        memory.append({\n            'last_trial': e['last_trial'],\n            'reflection': e['reflection'],\n            'signature': e['signature'],\n            'success': e['success']\n        })\n        signatures.append(e['signature'])\n    return {'memory': memory, 'signatures': signatures}\n\nNow escape for JSON: replace backslash with \\\\, double quote with \\\", newline with \\n, tab with \\t (none). The quotes inside the code are single quotes mostly, except for the error messages which use double quotes. So we need to escape those double quotes. Also the f-string has double quotes. So we need to replace each \" with \\\". Also backslashes in the f-string: there are none. Also the lambda uses colon and parentheses fine.\n\nLet's produce the string by manually escaping. I'll write the code as one line with \\n between lines. Each line indentation spaces remain.\n\nStart: \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be dict\\\")\\n    if 'capacity' not in case or 'trials' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing capacity or trials\\\")\\n    capacity = case['capacity']\\n    trials = case['trials']\\n    if not isinstance(capacity, int) or capacity < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"capacity must be non-negative integer\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(trials, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"trials must be list\\\")\\n    entries = []\\n    for i, trial in enumerate(trials):\\n        if not isinstance(trial, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each trial must be dict\\\")\\n        for key in ('signature','reflection','success'):\\n            if key not in trial:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"missing {key} in trial\\\")\\n        entries.append({\\n            'last_trial': i,\\n            'signature': trial['signature'],\\n            'reflection': trial['reflection'